Ultimately, our main goals are two-fold: (1) to complete resident-led research projects within challenging timeframes and (2) to train residents
in research methods and collaboration along the way. In order to be successful, resident collaboration and training must not only be effective but
efficient as well. This efficiency is achieved through a highly developed collaboration model and through the delivery of training materials to
residents, who tend to be relatively inexperienced in clinical research. Our collaboration model includes multiple templates for residents, which
assist them in visualizing what is required and provides them with ready-to-use structure to perform their work and to communicate with
biostatisticians on the team. The educational content and delivery is intended to limit time-consuming 1–1 instruction in essential topics and to
replace it with asynchronous self-study materials, which were specially designed with this target audience in mind. In essence, what has been
described here is an integrated system to help meet the above goals. We continue to develop this collaboration team model and resident training
material and have been encouraged by the results to date. We recommend this approach to other biostatistics collaboration units who are
engaged in supporting resident-led research.
