Kelsey Stilley is the Pharmacy Coordinator for Education and Professional Development at Duke University Hospital. Within this role, she
serves as the Coordinator for the Pharmacy Services Oversight Organization and is Chair of the Pharmacy Research Committee. She currently
oversees the pharmacy research process in collaboration with the Duke Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Research Design (BERD) Methods
Core for 22 pharmacy residents.
Jesse D. Troy is an Associate Professor in the Department of Biostatistics and Bioinformatics and the Associate Director of Graduate Studies
for the Masters of Biostatistics Program at Duke University. Dr. Troy also teaches biostatistics to physician scientists in the Clinical Research
Training Program at Duke, and he collaborates on research studies in cancer therapeutics and palliative care at the Duke Cancer Institute.
Tracy Truong is a Senior Biostatistician and Assistant Director of the Biostatistics, Epidemiology, and Research Design (BERD) Methods Core
at Duke University. She oversees the BERD Analytic Resources Navigation process, which connects investigators with existing quantitative
resources or methodologists with specific quantitative expertise. Furthermore, she leads the development of guidelines, best practices and
tools for BERD staff to ensure effective and efficient collaboration.
Steven C. Grambow is an Associate Professor and Associate Chair for Education in the Department of Biostatistics and Bioinformatics at
Duke University School of Medicine. He directs the Duke Clinical Research Training Program (CRTP), a 2-year professional degree program
designed for health professionals pursuing clinical and translational research careers. Additionally, he is the Co-Director of the Education and
Training Programs Pillar for the Duke Clinical and Translational Science Institute (CTSI). More about his work can be found on his Duke
scholar profile: https://scholars.duke.edu/person/steven.grambow.
Gina-Maria Pomann is an Associate Professor of Biostatistics and Bioinformatics and the Director of the Biostatistics, Epidemiology and
Research Design (BERD) Methods Core at Duke University, Durham, NC. The BERD Methods Core is a team of over 50 student, staff and fac
ulty biostatisticians and data scientists in the Department of Biostatistics and Bioinformatics who collaborate with clinical and/or translational
researchers. Duke BERD website: https://biostat.duke.edu/research/biostatistics-epidemiology-and-research-design-berd-methods-core.
